plugin-hostd (0.22.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * release: a push builds the deb for arm64 alone, as its qualification-db
    Build-Depends is (#301)
  * lint: the pull request body check runs where pull requests run (#300)
  * ci: the installed-package smoke tests install python3-plugin-hostd-client
  * ci: the installed-package smoke tests copy no data/ directory
  * release dry run: a dispatch off main builds against the staging channel
  * check-contract-dir: validate beside the caller's path, never this
    checkout's contract.d
  * tests/curve_reply: a term's unit is matched against OMX_CURVE_UNIT_WORDS
  * ci: the staging reads and the provenance guard share one condition; the
    trigger gate names lint.yml
  * ci: a dispatch off main reads the staging channel the wave stages to
  * Makefile: install-contract installs the whole of plugin-hostd-contract
  * packaging: the contract package is named in full, %package -n
    plugin-hostd-contract
  * tests: the readers and the render check follow the contract directory
    with no schema-major level
  * The contract directory has no schema-major level: the package is
    <contractdir>/plugin-hostd/
  * Every domain starts again at 0.1.0: info.version and each x-since (owner,
    2026-11-25)
  * tests: the verbs contract reads the protocol's one host-verbs header, and
    fake-host spells no patch_set line
  * tests/verbs_declared.py: description_get has its line, answered from a
    descriptions store of the run's own
  * tests/probe_domain.py: the probe domain's version is its owner's to give,
    no number of it is typed here
  * After the fold: the PRs that never met are made to agree
  * probe: the figure step with no map is OUT(CHILD_PROTOCOL), the outcome's
    name in the wave
  * tests: each word is read from its one home (ruling R5), and the guide
    follows the protocol's wave
  * qualification pin-from test: each domain an owner's manifest lists is
    staged beside it
  * .githooks/commit-msg: the shared stub again, byte for byte
  * bench.yml: a dispatch only
  * ci.yml: run the shared trigger gate
  * release: a merge to devel publishes the real package to staging
  * ci: a pull request into devel accepts staged omx packages; every other
    run still refuses them (#295)
  * lv2: the unit words are omx-contract 3.22.0's unit ids, percent and coef
